        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: aee75ec93771eedc6391a141a5fbdc3613409dcba611e39db2e0be67f47b8953\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: b61d3acf092c40bed15b5ef81c69c66c49476a70de4a4d530cf582aed2fb7356\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Step 1: Configure the ACL to deny packets with multicast administratively scoped destination addresses as shown in the example below.\n\nRP/0/0/CPU0:R2(config)#Ipv4 access-list MULTICAST_SCOPE\nRP/0/0/CPU0:R2(config-ipv4-acl)#deny 239.0.0.0 0.255.255.255\nRP/0/0/CPU0:R2(config-ipv4-acl)#permit any\n\nStep 2: Apply the multicast boundary at the appropriate interfaces as shown in the example below.\n\nRP/0/0/CPU0:R2(config)#multicast-routing \nRP/0/0/CPU0:R2(config-mcast)#address-family ipv4\nRP/0/0/CPU0:R2(config-mcast-default-ipv4)#int g0/0/0/1\nRP/0/0/CPU0:R2(config-mcast-default-ipv4-if)#boundary MULTICAST_SCOPE\nRP/0/0/CPU0:R2(config-mcast-default-ipv4-if)#end",
          "group_id": "V-216809",
          "group_id_src": "V-216809",
          "group_title": "SRG-NET-000019-RTR-000005",
          "rule_id": "SV-216809r1117237_rule",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-216809r1117237_rule",
          "rule_title": "The Cisco multicast edge router must be configured to establish boundaries for administratively scoped multicast traffic.",
          "rule_version": "CISC-RT-000810",
          "severity": "low",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "stig_uuid": "3d9ce002-ff6c-5afc-8d8e-b0e85a7a4431",
          "uuid": "6c18833a-451b-5d1b-8c84-78cd36e9b79b",
          "weight": "10.0"
